{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Then he sang.</b> He agreed to sing." "<b>For He is highly exalted.</b> To Him alone belongs the exaltation, to ascribe to Him the good that exists — and not to Pharaoh, the great dragon who said, יְאֹרִי וַאֲנִי עֲשִׂיתָנִי — \"The Nile is mine and I made myself\" (Ezekiel 29:3)." "<b>Horse and rider He hurled into the sea.</b> Pharaoh's horse and its rider, as it says (Psalms 136:15): וְנִעֵר פַּרְעֹה וְחֵילוֹ בְיַם סוּף — \"and swept Pharaoh and his army into the Sea of Reeds.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:34.364889877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}